{"id":"h271","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Neptune was discovered in 1781.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The claim that Neptune was discovered in 1781 is false.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Neptune was discovered in 1846 by Galle and d'Arrest at the Berlin Observatory.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Le Verrier and Adams predicted Neptune's position from irregularities in Uranus's orbit.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"1781 is a real and significant date in astronomy because Herschel discovered Uranus then.","confidence":0.97,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.5237,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The confusion likely arises because Uranus was the first planet found with a telescope and the two discoveries are often mentioned together.","confidence":0.7,"lean":-0.2,"theta":1.0996,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Neptune was identified about 65 years after 1781.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Herschel's 1781 observation concerned Uranus, not Neptune.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The claim misattributes Uranus's discovery date to Neptune.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.6,"relation":"